Third-party programs installed by the Helm chart
------------------------------------------------

The Kamerton Helm chart (deploy/helm/kamerton) installs the following
programs as dependencies, from their upstream Helm charts and container
images, unmodified. They are separate programs, distributed by their own
authors under their own licences; Kamerton only configures them through
their public interfaces (Kubernetes resources and HTTP APIs).

  Program                   Licence      Installed through the chart
  Prometheus                Apache-2.0   kube-prometheus-stack (prometheus-community)
  Prometheus Operator       Apache-2.0   kube-prometheus-stack (prometheus-community)
  Alertmanager              Apache-2.0   kube-prometheus-stack (prometheus-community)
  OpenTelemetry Collector   Apache-2.0   opentelemetry-collector (open-telemetry)
  Grafana                   AGPL-3.0     grafana (grafana-community)
  Loki                      AGPL-3.0     loki (grafana-community)
  Tempo                     AGPL-3.0     tempo (grafana-community)
  OpenTelemetry eBPF        Apache-2.0   opentelemetry-ebpf-instrumentation (open-telemetry),
    Instrumentation (OBI)                optional, off by default (autoInstrument.enabled)

Chart versions are pinned in deploy/helm/kamerton/Chart.yaml. The upstream
charts may install further components (for example kube-state-metrics and
node-exporter in kube-prometheus-stack); see each chart for its contents and
licences.

Libraries compiled into the Kamerton binary and the web UI are listed with
their versions in go.mod / go.sum and web/package.json / web/pnpm-lock.yaml;
each keeps its own licence.

